The implementation will use the direct repeated-division algorithm: prepend `str(x % base)` while `x > 0`, then return the accumulated string. This stays inside the translator’s supported subset and matches the prompt’s examples; the formal domain will need to state the meaningful base range (`2 <= base < 10`) and nonnegative input explicitly.
