One proof-design adjustment is warranted before freezing the program: using Python’s `chr(48 + digit)` avoids making the theorem depend on symbolic behavior of K’s host `Int2String` hook. It computes the same one-character digit for bases 2–9, while the supplied semantics defines `chr` directly, keeping the proof inside the reference model’s explicit rules.
